<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n60541" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κῡδ-αίνω</span></b> , fut.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κυδᾰνῶ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lyc.
					721
				</span></i>
			, etc.: 
				Ep.
			
			aor.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κύδηνα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					23.793
				</span></i>
			; 
				Dor.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκύδᾱνα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>P.</u>
					1.31
				</span></i>
			: (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κῦδος</span>):—<i>give</i>
			or <i>do honour to</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινα</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				10.69
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				13.348
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				350
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠμὲν κυδῆναι θνητὸν βροτὸν ἠδὲ
					κακῶσαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					16.212
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ζεύς, ὅς μιν . . τίμα καὶ κύδαινε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					15.612
				</span></i>
			; [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Αἰνείαν] ἀκέοντό τε κύδαινόν
				τε</span> they healed and <i>glorified</i> him, by
			restoring strength and beauty, <i><span class="en">
				5.448
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πάλᾳ κυδαίνων Τεγέαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>O.</u>
					10(11).66
				</span></i>
			, cf.<i><span class="en">
				<u>P.</u>
				1.31
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πατρίδα κ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Simon.
					151
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σφ᾽ ἀρετὴ κυδαίνουσ᾽ ἀνάγει . . ἐξ
					Ἀΐδεω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					99.4
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρὸ τοῦ κήπου κ. τὸν περίπατον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.635a
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>delight</i> or <i>gladden by marks of honour</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κύδαινε δὲ θυμὸν ἄνακτος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					14.438
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				23.793
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> seldom in
			bad sense, <i>flatter, fawn upon</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Op.</u>
				38
			</span></i>, cj. in <i><span class="en">
				Max.Tyr.
				20.1
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b>
			
				Med.
			, <i>pride oneself</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ πατράσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Onos.
					1.24
				</span></i>
			.—Poet. and late Prose.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
